  "title": "Mind in Motion Young Adults Walking Over Uneven Terrain",
  "description": "A multimodal mobile brain/body imaging dataset from 32 young adults walking over uneven terrain at different speeds. It includes high-density dual-layer EEG, neck EMG, IMU acceleration, ground reaction forces, and head models built from T1-weighted MR images. Each participant also completed a seated rest trial, and digitized electrode locations are provided for every subject.",
  "methods_description": "Participants completed two three-minute trials for each terrain and speed condition, plus a three-minute seated rest trial. Recordings comprised dual-layer EEG, neck EMG, IMU acceleration, and ground reaction forces. Digitized electrode locations and T1 structural MRI were used to construct head models.",
